  "notes": "Hand-transcribed 2026-10-02 from the official Elon University Department of Nursing 'Elon ABSN Curriculum' page (elon.edu). The Accelerated Bachelor of Science in Nursing (ABSN) is an intensive 16-month post-baccalaureate program: 67 credit hours and 540 clinical hours, laid out term-by-term as Fall I, Winter Term I, Spring I, Summer I and II, Fall II. Term subtotals 17+4+17+11+18=67 match the published curriculum total; clinical hours 90+0+160+40+250=540. Admission requires an earned bachelor's degree in another field plus 18-24 hours of prerequisite coursework (anatomy, physiology, microbiology, statistics, human growth and development, nutrition) completed prior to admission -- these are admission requirements, not part of the sequenced plan. program_type 'accelerated': accelerated second-degree track; 5 terms within the 2-7 gate. Course prerequisites are not published on the curriculum page; prereq arrays left empty per the no-invention rule.",
